{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and motion as separate plants, then use compact specifications to map clear sensing to forward-progress actions and obstacle sensing to one-shot recovery actions. The policy favors move_forward in clear space, uses random_walk only as a secondary exploration mode, applies directed turns away from side obstacles, and uses a brief move_backward only for front-obstacle escape before quickly returning to forward exploration. Action states self-loop on path_clear so intended open-loop pulses are not preempted by non-critical sensing updates.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability",
    "Use perception/decision states plus one-shot action/recovery states",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward, with random_walk as a secondary clear-space option",
    "Use rotate_clockwise for obstacle_left and rotate_counterclockwise for obstacle_right consistently",
    "Use move_backward only after obstacle_front and only as a single brief escape pulse",
    "Return to clear exploration immediately on path_clear after recovery when safe",
    "Make all states total with respect to uncontrollable events and deterministic"
  ],
